From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenHD <openhd@openhd.org>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 13:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: enable RK356x VOP2 multi-area windows

The RK3568 Android device tree enables support-multi-area on the VOP2
node, but the common RK356x device tree leaves it disabled. On RK3566
ground-station displays this limits the exposed KMS plane set to the
primary, one Esmart cursor/overlay, and one cluster overlay.

Enable the multi-area path for the normal RK356x device tree too. This
allows the Rockchip DRM driver to expose additional VOP2 subwindows where
the hardware and plane registration rules allow it, which gives low-latency
KMS compositors more options for separating video, OSD, and UI surfaces.

Signed-off-by: OpenHD <openhd@openhd.org>
---
 src/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x.dtsi b/src/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x.dtsi
--- a/src/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x.dtsi
+++ b/src/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk356x.dtsi
@@ -1930,6 +1930,7 @@ vop: vop@fe040000 {
 		iommus = <&vop_mmu>;
 		power-domains = <&power RK3568_PD_VO>;
 		rockchip,grf = <&grf>;
+		support-multi-area;
 		status = "disabled";
 
 		vop_out: ports {
-- 
